{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5 now available on AWS - AWS","context":"AWS has introduced Claude Sonnet 5, Anthropic's latest and most capable Sonnet model, which offers top-tier intelligence at Sonnet pricing for coding, agents, and everyday professional work at scale. This model delivers strong performance across various tasks, including coding, where it navigates large codebases, lands multi-file changes, and carries debugging and refactoring tasks through to completion with fewer rounds of correction. For agents, it calls tools precisely, holds state across many steps, and recovers from errors to ensure more runs finish correctly the first time. For knowledge work, it builds spreadsheets, drafts documents, and turns unstructured material into structured analysis. Customers can access Claude Sonnet 5 through two methods: Amazon Bedrock and Claude Platform on AWS. Amazon Bedrock keeps data within AWS infrastructure and provides access to Claude Sonnet 5 through a unified service with AWS-managed features like Guardrails, Knowledge Bases, and regional data residency. Claude Platform on AWS offers direct access to Anthropic's native platform experience and capabilities via the AWS Console, allowing users to build, test, and deploy with the same APIs, features, and console experience as working with Anthropic directly, unified with AWS billing and authentication","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/06/claude-sonnet-5-now-available-on-aws/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 now available on AWS - AWS","context":"AWS has introduced Claude Sonnet 5.5, an advanced and cost-effective Sonnet for coding and knowledge work. Sonnet 5.5 offers improved efficiency and faster processing compared to Sonnet 5. Customers can access Claude Sonnet 5.5 through two methods: Amazon Bedrock and Claude Platform on AWS. Amazon Bedrock keeps data within AWS infrastructure, offers regional data residency, and includes AWS-managed features like Guardrails and Knowledge Bases. Claude Platform on AWS provides direct access to Anthropic's native platform experience and capabilities via the AWS Console, with unified billing and authentication","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/claude-sonnet-5-5-aws/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"amazon-bedrock","skill_description":"Builds generative AI applications on Amazon Bedrock. Covers model invocation (Converse API, InvokeModel), RAG with Knowledge Bases, Bedrock Agents, Guardrails, and AgentCore (including the Harness managed agent loop). Applies when invoking models, setting up or migrating Knowledge Bases to Managed, deploying to AgentCore, migrating/porting/converting a Bedrock Agent (including inline agents) to an AgentCore Harness, troubleshooting Bedrock errors (ThrottlingException, AccessDeniedException), or choosing Bedrock models (Claude, Llama, Nova, Titan). Also for prompt caching, quota and throttling diagnosis, cost tracking, migrating between Claude model generations, chunking strategies, and Bedrock model selection. Covers AgentCore Payments (x402, microtransactions, Payment Manager, Connector, Instrument, Coinbase CDP, Stripe Privy, paid endpoints, agent payments). NOT for custom model training, Rekognition, or Comprehend. For SageMaker model discovery, customization, or endpoints, use aws-ai-ml.\n\nServices: bedrock, bedrock-runtime, bedrock-mantle, bedrock-agent, bedrock-agent-runtime, bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, design, migrate\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: generative-ai, rag, agents","skill_name":"amazon-bedrock"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"caching-for-llm-inference","skill_description":"Sets up a shared L2 KV cache for self-hosted LLM inference on Amazon ElastiCache for Valkey, so GPU servers load prefill KV state over EFA RDMA instead of recomputing it. Checks fit, estimates savings with KVTrace, builds a business case, creates the cache, connects vLLM or SGLang (also as NVIDIA Dynamo or llm-d workers) through an LMCache server, tunes for cost or latency, and troubleshoots. Use when a builder serves open-weight models on GPUs (for example H100 or B200, on Amazon EC2 or Amazon EKS) for multi-turn chat, agents, RAG, or long contexts and asks about KV cache offloading, prefix cache sharing, prompt caching for self-hosted models, LMCache with Valkey, or lower TTFT or GPU cost. Not for Bedrock prompt caching, LLM response or semantic caching, or general application caching.\n\nServices: elasticache, ec2\nTasks: deploy, optimize, troubleshoot\nPersona: developer, data-scientist, devops\nWorkload: ai-ml","skill_name":"caching-for-llm-inference"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"storing-and-querying-vectors","skill_description":"Store and query vector embeddings using Amazon S3 Vectors, a cost-effective long-term vector storage service with its own API namespace (s3vectors). Triggers on: create S3 vector bucket, vector index, store embeddings, semantic search, RAG vector storage, similarity search, vector database, migrate from other vector databases. Do NOT use for: querying tabular data (use querying-data-lake), S3 object storage, or hundreds/thousands of sustained QPS (use OpenSearch).\n\n\nServices: s3vectors, bedrock\nTasks: deploy, debug, migrate\nPersona: developer, architect\nWorkload: data-analytics\n*","skill_name":"storing-and-querying-vectors"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search AWS docs for Bedrock Sonnet 5 pricing or promotions"}

